window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-4551b1fa8e7d0583"]={"key":"ny_c-4551b1fa8e7d0583","group":"ny_c","uid":"4551b1fa8e7d0583","rank":21,"title":"windermere dual legacy coa model","occupation":"accountants_auditors","archetype":"code_exec","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are Aleksy Vanterpool, the accountant seconded to Windermere Mutual to own the finance design following its 1 July merger with a Polish fabrication group. Six weeks of postings are sitting in suspense because the Irish and Polish charts agree only at their upper levels, and Henrik Sheridan needs one target account structure ready before the Q3 close opens so that the Sandpiper Board receives a consistent period comparison. Build an executable analytical model rather than a presentation: use `legacy_coa_and_balances.xlsx` for the two legacy account masters, representative balances, duplicate and malformed migration entries, and the locked subsidiary-ledger identifiers, and use `reporting_constraints.pdf` for the permitted target segments, Polish and Irish statutory rollups, SOX 404 control classes, product-margin requirements, constraint identifiers, and material-variance policy. The model must commit to one target structure and dual-legacy crosswalk that satisfies those constraints; balancing alone is not evidence that a mapping is appropriate. Package `coa_model.py` and `README.md` in `target_coa_model.zip`, and write that archive into the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename. The operating contract is as follows. (1) `coa_model.py` must expose `analyze(records, period_a, period_b)`, where `records` is a list of dictionaries using the workbook field names `row_id`, `legacy_system`, `entity_code`, `legacy_account`, `legacy_label`, `jurisdiction`, `product_code`, `period`, `amount_eur`, and `record_status`; the two period arguments are distinct strings in `YYYY-Qn` form, with `n` from 1 through 4, and the comparison direction is period B less period A. The function must not read the workbook during execution: the supplied rows or equivalent hidden rows will be passed directly to it. (2) Return a dictionary with exactly the top-level keys `status`, `periods`, `target_accounts`, `legacy_mapping`, `variances`, and `controls`. `periods` must identify `period_a` and `period_b`. Each target-account row must contain `target_account`, `target_label`, `natural_code`, `product_code`, `control_class`, `ie_stat_code`, `pl_stat_code`, and `constraint_ids`; each mapping row must contain `legacy_system`, `entity_code`, `legacy_account`, `product_code`, `target_account`, and `constraint_ids`. Each variance row must contain `target_account`, `period_a_amount_eur`, `period_b_amount_eur`, `change_eur`, `change_pct`, `material`, and `drivers`. Each driver must identify `legacy_system`, `legacy_account`, and `change_eur`. Controls must report included input and mapped output totals for both periods. (3) Treat surrounding whitespace and letter case as immaterial in codes, statuses, and labels, returning the canonical codes from the attachments. Labels are descriptive and must not cause otherwise identical account keys to map differently. Include `POSTED` and `SUSPENSE` records; exclude `VOID` and `TEST` records. An exact repeated `row_id`, after normalization and numeric parsing, is one record, while contradictory content under the same `row_id` must raise `ValueError` containing `CONFLICTING_DUPLICATE` and the row ID. Missing required fields, nonnumeric amounts, impossible field values, unknown relevant accounts, and unknown product codes are errors rather than rows to skip; raise `ValueError` containing respectively `INVALID_RECORD`, `UNMAPPED_ACCOUNT`, or `UNKNOWN_PRODUCT` as applicable. Invalid or equal period arguments must raise `ValueError` containing `INVALID_PERIOD`. (4) If all supplied records are valid but no included record belongs to either requested period, return `status` as `empty`, empty lists, and zero controls. This genuine empty result must remain distinct from every validation or mapping error. Otherwise return `status` as `ok`, preserve suspense amounts, apply the locked-ledger crosswalk without attempting to rewrite its source identifiers, and provide both statutory rollups, the SOX class, product dimension, and applicable constraint identifiers for every resulting target account. (5) Aggregate with decimal precision before presentation. Round euro outputs only after aggregation to two decimal places using round-half-up; calculate percentage change as `(period_b - period_a) / abs(period_a) * 100`, round it to one decimal place using round-half-up, and return `null` when period A is zero. Apply the materiality rule in the constraints document, and for each material variance return up to three source-account drivers ranked by absolute change, then by legacy system and account code for ties; nonmaterial rows have an empty driver list. Sort target accounts and variances by target account, and mappings by legacy system, entity, legacy account, and product code, so repeated calls are identical. Keep the findings factual: neither output nor README should recommend journal entries, controls, or management action. The README should briefly describe the chosen structure, the competing constraints it resolves, the assumptions separated from sourced requirements, the error and empty-result behavior, and where a maintainer changes mappings, segment definitions, and materiality without editing the same assumption in several places. The runtime is offline Python 3.11 using only the standard library.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/legacy_coa_and_balances.xlsx` — Provides both legacy charts, representative two-period balances, source identifiers, product codes, suspense postings, and imperfect migration records used to design and exercise the crosswalk.\n- `references/reporting_constraints.pdf` — Defines the permitted target segments and canonical codes, Irish and Polish statutory rollups, SOX control classes, product-margin requirements, constraint identifiers, and the material-variance policy.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `target_coa_model.zip` — Executable dual-legacy chart-of-accounts mapping and period-variance model, containing `coa_model.py` and `README.md`. (Place the archive at the top level of the working directory. It must contain `coa_model.py` exposing `analyze(records, period_a, period_b)` and `README.md`. Code must run offline under Python 3.11 using only the standard library and must not read the supplied workbook or PDF at runtime.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/legacy_coa_and_balances.xlsx","bytes":6833,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/8abbc1f662268d81bc1f006c7067cc8688b1581ee7a647f654c4b85376167c26.xlsx","sha256":"8abbc1f662268d81bc1f006c7067cc8688b1581ee7a647f654c4b85376167c26","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Migration export","row_count":30,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Windermere Mutual — legacy balances export"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Q3 close integration | exported 2026-08-20"]},{"r":"4","cells":["row_id","legacy_system","entity_code","legacy_account","legacy_label","jurisdiction","product_code","period","amount_eur","record_status"]},{"r":"5","cells":["IE-001"," IE_GL ","ie01","1000","Cash at bank"," ie ","p1","2026-Q2","1000.005","posted"]},{"r":"6","cells":["IE-002","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Product revenue","IE","P1","2026-Q2","25000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"7","cells":["IE-003","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Revenue — widgets","IE","P1","2026-Q3","27500.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"8","cells":["IE-004","IE_GL","IE01","5000","Cost of sales","IE","P1","2026-Q3","-12000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"9","cells":["IE-005","IE_GL","IE01","6100","Factory overhead","IE","P2","2026-Q3","-3100.005","SUSPENSE"]},{"r":"10","cells":["IE-006","IE_GL","IE01","1200","Trade receivables","IE","P2","2026-Q3","8000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"11","cells":["IE-007","IE_GL","IE01","2100","Trade creditors","IE","P2","2026-Q3","-4200.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"12","cells":["IE-008","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Sales (translated)","IE","P2","2026-Q3","5000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"13","cells":["IE-009","IE_GL","IE01","1000","Cash","IE","P1","2026-Q3","0.005","POSTED"]},{"r":"14","cells":["IE-010","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Revenue","IE","P1","2026-Q3","0.005","POSTED"]},{"r":"15","cells":["IE-011","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Revenue","IE","P1","2026-Q3","0.005","POSTED"]},{"r":"16","cells":["IE-012","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Revenue","IE","P1","2026-Q3","9999","VOID"]},{"r":"17","cells":["IE-013","IE_GL","IE01","4000","Revenue","IE","P1","2026-Q3","9999","TEST"]},{"r":"18","cells":["PL-001","PL_FK","PL01","7001","Sprzedaż wyrobów","PL","P1","2026-Q2","18000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"19","cells":["PL-002","PL_FK","PL01","7001","Przychody ze sprzedazy","PL","P1","2026-Q3","21000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"20","cells":["PL-003","PL_FK","PL01","7300","Koszt materiałów","PL","P1","2026-Q3","-9000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"21","cells":["PL-004","PL_FK","PL01","5500","Koszty wydziałowe","PL","P2","2026-Q3","-2400.00","SUSPENSE"]},{"r":"22","cells":["PL-005","PL_FK","PL01","1300","Należności handlowe","PL","P2","2026-Q3","6000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"23","cells":["PL-006","PL_FK","PL01","2001","Zobowiązania","PL","P2","2026-Q3","-3000.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"24","cells":["PL-007","PL_FK","PL01","9998","Locked subsidiary ledger","PL","P1","2026-Q3","750.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"25","cells":["PL-008","PL_FK","PL01","7001","Sales duplicate","PL","P1","2026-Q3","100.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"26","cells":["PL-008","PL_FK","PL01","7001","Sales duplicate","PL","P1","2026-Q3","100.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"27","cells":["PL-009","PL_FK","PL01","7001","Sales conflicting","PL","P1","2026-Q3","101.00","POSTED"]},{"r":"28","cells":["IE-014","IE_GL","IE01","1000","Cash","IE","P9","2026-Q3","50","POSTED"]},{"r":"29","cells":["IE-015","IE_GL","IE01","1000","Cash","IE","P1","2026-Q1","oops","POSTED"]},{"r":"30","cells":["IE-016","IE_GL","IE01","1000","Cash","IE","P1","2026-Q1","10","VOID"]},{"r":"31","cells":["IE-017","IE_GL","IE01","1000","Cash","IE","P1","2026-Q1","10","POSTED"]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/reporting_constraints.pdf","bytes":2554,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/1f40ae9a5e59fc7cea74bf4d9f383ffaa6666742633fc4afe73ff69b2d0adec4.pdf","sha256":"1f40ae9a5e59fc7cea74bf4d9f383ffaa6666742633fc4afe73ff69b2d0adec4","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"Windermere Mutual — Q3 reporting constraints (rev 1.4)\nTarget account syntax: ENTITY-NATURAL-PRODUCT-CONTROL. Canonical entities: IE01 (Irish), PL01 (Polish).\nNatural segments: 1000 Cash; 1200 Trade receivables; 2100 Trade payables; 4000 Revenue; 5000 Cost of sales; 6100 Operating expen\nProducts: P1 Fabrication; P2 Components; GEN Shared/overhead. Product is mandatory for revenue and cost accounts; use GEN for ba\nControl classes: C01 SOX key balance; C02 SOX revenue; C03 SOX inventory/cost; C04 SOX operating expense.\nIrish statutory rollups: IE-CASH, IE-AR, IE-AP, IE-REV, IE-COGS, IE-OPEX respectively by natural code.\nPolish statutory rollups: PL-100, PL-120, PL-200, PL-700, PL-730, PL-550 respectively by natural code.\nProduct-margin reporting requires P1/P2 retained on 4000 and 5000; GEN is not permitted for those classes.\nConstraint register: CT-SEG (segment vocabulary/syntax); CT-IE (Irish statutory); CT-PL (Polish statutory); CT-SOX (control class); CT-M\nFrozen-ledger account PL_FK/PL01/9998 is a subsidiary identifier and must remain unchanged in source mapping.\nMaterial variance: material when absolute change >= EUR 1,000 OR (period A non-zero and absolute percentage change >= 10.0%). Thr\nAlternative mappings that merely balance are not acceptable if they collapse products, lose statutory rollups, misclassify SOX controls, or\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/target_coa_model.zip","bytes":3430,"extension":".zip","url":"assets/8a9a4fe2e76cab8a31c0bcbed43a20df07ce3e827a4cf73e71b0c89678ca2339.zip","sha256":"8a9a4fe2e76cab8a31c0bcbed43a20df07ce3e827a4cf73e71b0c89678ca2339","preview":{"kind":"unavailable","note":"此格式未做网页解析，原文件可下载。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The execution harness can call `analyze(records, period_a, period_b)` with the documented three arguments and receives a dictionary rather than process output or an interactive workflow.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Imported submission and hidden valid input","grader_hint":"Load the submitted module in an isolated Python 3.11 process, call the entry point positionally, and inspect the returned Python object."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A nonempty valid case returns `status` equal to `ok` and exactly the documented six top-level keys.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden valid two-period case","grader_hint":"Compare the returned key set exactly and verify the status value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The returned periods identify the supplied period A and period B without reversing the comparison direction.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden case using distinguishable quarter strings","grader_hint":"Call with two distinct periods and verify the period metadata and subsequent B-minus-A arithmetic."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Irish legacy account records map to target accounts satisfying the permitted segment vocabulary and their applicable crosswalk constraints.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden Irish account cases derived from the supplied sources","grader_hint":"Exercise representative Irish natural-account and product combinations and validate target segments and mapping relationships against the constraint register."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Polish legacy account records map to target accounts satisfying the permitted segment vocabulary and their applicable crosswalk constraints.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden Polish account cases derived from the supplied sources","grader_hint":"Exercise representative Polish account and product combinations, including accounts whose lower-level labels differ from Irish labels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every produced target account decomposes consistently into the documented entity, natural, product, and control segment conventions.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Target-account rows from hidden mixed-system cases","grader_hint":"Parse each target identifier using the supplied segment convention and compare its components with the row attributes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A normalized legacy-system, entity, account, and product key maps to exactly one target account.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden cases with repeated postings for the same mapping key","grader_hint":"Group mapping rows by the documented source key and assert one distinct target identifier per key."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The locked subsidiary-ledger source account identifiers are retained in the legacy mapping while their postings receive valid target dimensions.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden records from the frozen ledger population","grader_hint":"Verify source identifiers remain unchanged in mapping rows and that target assignment uses a crosswalk rather than a rewritten source account."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Distinct valid product codes remain distinguishable in target accounts and product-margin aggregation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two otherwise identical records with different valid products","grader_hint":"Confirm the records produce distinct product dimensions and do not collapse into one target account."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Target accounts carry the correct Irish statutory rollup code where the supplied constraints require one.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden target accounts spanning Irish statutory categories","grader_hint":"Compare `ie_stat_code` with the relational rollup prescribed for each tested natural-account class."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Target accounts carry the correct Polish statutory rollup code where the supplied constraints require one.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden target accounts spanning Polish statutory categories","grader_hint":"Compare `pl_stat_code` with the relational rollup prescribed for each tested natural-account class."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The SOX control class assigned to each tested target account agrees with the relevant reporting constraint.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden accounts from multiple control classes","grader_hint":"Validate `control_class` against the account characteristics and constraint register, not against account balance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Constraint identifiers returned for target and mapping rows exist in the supplied register and include the constraints that actually force the tested segment or crosswalk choice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Constraint traces from hidden mapping cases","grader_hint":"Reject invented IDs and traces that omit a directly applicable statutory, control, margin, or frozen-ledger constraint."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Changes in descriptive legacy labels do not alter the mapping of otherwise identical normalized keys.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Paired hidden records with inconsistent labels","grader_hint":"Vary capitalization, language, and descriptive wording while holding the source key fixed; compare target assignments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Surrounding whitespace and case differences in codes, statuses, and labels are normalized to the canonical supplied codes.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden records containing padded and mixed-case fields","grader_hint":"Compare results with an equivalent clean input and inspect canonical codes in the output."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An exactly duplicated row ID with equivalent normalized content is counted once.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden duplicate pair","grader_hint":"Compare controls and variances with a single-record run; totals must not double."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Contradictory normalized content under one row ID raises `ValueError` containing `CONFLICTING_DUPLICATE` and the affected row ID.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden conflicting duplicate","grader_hint":"Change an amount or mapping field while repeating the row ID and inspect exception type and message."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"`POSTED` and `SUSPENSE` records are included in totals and mappings.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden case containing both included statuses","grader_hint":"Calculate the expected included total from both statuses and compare with controls and mapped balances."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"`VOID` and `TEST` records are excluded from totals, mappings, variances, and drivers.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden case containing large excluded-status amounts","grader_hint":"Use conspicuous excluded amounts and verify they affect no returned analytical value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A missing required field, nonnumeric amount, or impossible field value raises `ValueError` containing `INVALID_RECORD` rather than being silently skipped.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Multiple hidden malformed-record cases","grader_hint":"Test each malformed class separately and confirm no partial result is returned."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An unknown relevant legacy account raises `ValueError` containing `UNMAPPED_ACCOUNT`.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden validly formed but unmapped source account","grader_hint":"Use an included-status record in a requested period so the unknown account cannot be treated as irrelevant."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An unknown product code raises `ValueError` containing `UNKNOWN_PRODUCT`.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden validly formed record with an unsupported product","grader_hint":"Use a known legacy account and requested period to isolate product validation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Malformed period arguments or two equal periods raise `ValueError` containing `INVALID_PERIOD`.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden malformed, out-of-range-quarter, and equal-period calls","grader_hint":"Exercise each documented invalid period condition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Valid input with no included records in either requested period returns the defined genuine empty result rather than raising an exception.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden valid records from other periods","grader_hint":"Verify `status` is `empty`, analytical lists are empty, and all controls are zero."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Validation and mapping errors remain errors even when the affected record is outside the requested periods, preserving the distinction from a genuine empty result.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden malformed and unmapped records outside the requested periods","grader_hint":"Confirm the documented exception is raised rather than returning `empty`."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Numeric strings, integers, floats, and decimal-compatible values are aggregated without premature binary precision loss.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden mixed numeric representations including fractional cents","grader_hint":"Compare output with a Decimal-based reference calculation performed before rounding."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Euro totals and changes are rounded only after aggregation to two decimal places using round-half-up.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden half-cent and accumulation boundary cases","grader_hint":"Use values for which row-level rounding, banker's rounding, and aggregate half-up produce different answers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Percentage change uses B minus A over the absolute value of A, is rounded to one decimal place using round-half-up, and is null when A is zero.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden positive, negative-base, half-way, and zero-base cases","grader_hint":"Check each boundary independently against Decimal reference arithmetic."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material flags agree with the materiality rule in the reporting constraints, including values exactly on each stated threshold.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden below-threshold, on-threshold, and above-threshold variances","grader_hint":"Generate cases around every absolute and percentage boundary stated in the supplied policy."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material variances contain no more than three source-account drivers ordered by absolute change, with the documented lexical tie-breaks.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden material variance with more than three contributors and tied changes","grader_hint":"Compare selected and ordered drivers with an independently aggregated source-account ranking."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Nonmaterial variance rows have an empty driver list.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden nonmaterial variance with several contributing records","grader_hint":"Confirm contributors are not emitted as drivers when the material flag is false."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Included input totals equal mapped output totals for each period within ±0.01 EUR, and controls reflect the same included population used by variances.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hidden mixed-system, mixed-status, two-period case","grader_hint":"Independently sum normalized included records by period and compare input controls, output controls, and mapped variance totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Target accounts, variances, mappings, and drivers follow the documented deterministic sort orders, and repeated calls with equivalent input ordering return equal objects.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Shuffled hidden records and repeated calls","grader_hint":"Run several input permutations and compare complete returned objects and each list's key order."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The chosen target structure and its constraint traces form a coherent, maintainable accounting design rather than merely a balancing crosswalk.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Executable outputs, implementation organization, and submitted maintainer documentation","grader_hint":"Review whether statutory rollups, SOX classes, product visibility, and the frozen-ledger constraint are resolved consistently and whether traces explain the forcing constraints."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"Sourced requirements and implementation assumptions are clearly distinguishable, and mappings, segment definitions, and materiality can each be maintained from a single logical location.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Implementation structure and maintainer documentation","grader_hint":"Inspect whether a maintainer could change one assumption without searching for duplicated literals or reconciling conflicting descriptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The model and documentation present factual mapping and variance information without recommending entries, controls, or management action.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Returned labels and traces plus maintainer documentation","grader_hint":"Allow neutral descriptions of effects and constraints; withhold credit for prescriptive recommendations."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Windermere Mutual is integrating Irish and Polish finance records after a midyear merger while preserving statutory, SOX, product-margin, and frozen-ledger requirements. The model will support CFO and Sandpiper Board review of the Q3 close without proposing management action.","difficulty_sources":["Committing to one account structure when several alternatives balance but do not satisfy the same statutory, control, margin, and frozen-ledger constraints","Normalizing imperfect migration records without concealing malformed or contradictory data","Maintaining traceability from both legacy systems to target segments and jurisdictional rollups","Producing deterministic period comparisons with explicit empty, error, materiality, and rounding boundaries"],"authoring_plan":{"reference_materials":{"legacy_workbook":{"content_requirements":["Provide two legacy account masters and representative balances for two comparison periods using the exact input-field vocabulary stated in the request.","Include ordinary posted rows, migration suspense rows, exact duplicate row IDs, one contradictory duplicate, malformed amounts or required fields, excluded statuses, inconsistent casing and whitespace, translated or inconsistent labels, and accounts from a ledger whose identifiers cannot be re-segmented.","Include multiple products, natural-account classes, control classes, statutory categories, positive and negative balances, a zero-base comparison, and fractional-cent values that distinguish aggregate round-half-up from row rounding and binary-float arithmetic.","Keep malformed and contradictory examples visibly identifiable as migration-quality examples so a practitioner can understand that the executable must reject rather than map them."],"relationships":["For all included valid records, the source mapping key is legacy system, entity, legacy account, and product.","Labels never determine the mapping key.","Exact duplicates are equivalent after trimming, canonical case normalization, and decimal parsing.","The locked ledger retains its source account identifiers and obtains target dimensions through the crosswalk."]},"constraint_document":{"content_requirements":["Define canonical entity, natural, product, and control segment code sets and the syntax for composing a target account.","Define relational Irish and Polish statutory rollups by natural-account class.","Define SOX control-class assignments and the product-margin dimension that must survive mapping.","Assign stable constraint identifiers to each substantive requirement, including the frozen-ledger requirement.","State one materiality policy with both absolute and percentage boundaries and make inclusion at an exact threshold unambiguous.","Present at least two superficially balancing mapping alternatives whose weakness appears only when statutory, control, product, or frozen-ledger constraints are considered; do not provide a completed target crosswalk."]}},"interface":{"runtime":"Offline Python 3.11 standard library only","entrypoint":"analyze(records, period_a, period_b) -> dict","input":"A list of dictionaries with the exact ten fields stated in the request and two distinct YYYY-Q1 through YYYY-Q4 period strings.","output":"A dictionary with the exact top-level and row-level fields stated in the request.","determinism":"No network, wall-clock dependency, environment-dependent ordering, randomness, or mutable cross-call state."},"gold_design":{"target_structure":["Select one four-segment target design using the canonical entity, natural, product, and control vocabularies.","Map both legacy systems into the same natural-account taxonomy while preserving separate statutory rollup attributes for both jurisdictions.","Keep product as an explicit target dimension rather than inferring it from mutable labels.","For the frozen ledger, preserve the source account in mapping output and derive target dimensions only through a maintained crosswalk.","Attach every applicable supplied constraint ID to target-account and mapping rows."],"calculation_rules":["Normalize surrounding whitespace and case before validation and key comparison; return canonical reference codes.","Include POSTED and SUSPENSE and exclude VOID and TEST.","Deduplicate normalized-equivalent repeated row IDs; reject contradictory repeated IDs.","Validate every supplied record before deciding whether the requested periods have data, so out-of-period defects remain errors.","Aggregate using Decimal, calculate B minus A, then apply two-decimal euro and one-decimal percentage round-half-up conventions.","Use absolute period-A amount as the percentage denominator and null when period A is zero.","Apply the documented materiality boundaries inclusively.","Rank material drivers after aggregation by absolute change descending, then canonical legacy system and account ascending; return at most three.","Control totals equal the included normalized source population and its mapped output by period."],"empty_and_error_contract":["A valid population with no included records in either requested period returns status empty, empty analytical lists, and zero controls.","Invalid periods, malformed records, contradictory duplicates, unknown relevant accounts, and unknown products raise the documented ValueError categories and never return empty or a partial result."]},"hidden_tests":{"approach":"Create property-oriented tests from the supplied vocabularies and relationships rather than comparing the entire result with one literal fixture.","cases":["Representative Irish and Polish mappings across natural, product, statutory, and control categories.","Frozen-ledger source identifier preservation.","Label variations, mixed case, and padded codes.","Exact and contradictory duplicates.","All four record statuses.","Missing fields, nonnumeric values, impossible codes, unmapped accounts, and unknown products.","Malformed, equal, and valid period arguments.","Valid genuine-empty input and defective out-of-period input.","Mixed numeric representations, aggregate half-cent boundaries, percentage half-way boundaries, negative period-A values, and zero period-A values.","Materiality values below, exactly on, and above each boundary.","More than three drivers and lexical ties.","Input permutations and repeated calls.","Per-period reconciliation between included input, mapped output, and variance amounts."],"naive_solution_rejection":["A label-based crosswalk fails inconsistent-label tests.","A solution that merely balances but omits statutory, control, product, or trace attributes fails mapping-property tests.","Float arithmetic or row-level rounding fails precision boundaries.","Silently skipped malformed records fail explicit error tests.","Filtering periods before validation fails out-of-period error tests.","Re-segmenting the frozen source identifiers fails preservation tests.","Hard-coded fixture totals fail generated amount and ordering tests."],"reference_validation":"Run the reference implementation from a clean interpreter against the complete hidden suite, then mutate amounts, row order, labels, products, statuses, and boundary values to confirm tests validate behavior rather than one fixture. Confirm a plausible balance-only, label-matching implementation fails materially."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"mixed_media_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"legacy_coa_balances","filename":"legacy_coa_and_balances.xlsx","purpose":"Provides both legacy charts, representative two-period balances, source identifiers, product codes, suspense postings, and imperfect migration records used to design and exercise the crosswalk.","required":true,"discovery":"Review the account-master and balance information together; the same source keys and codes are used in the records passed to the executable entry point."},{"artifact_id":"reporting_constraints","filename":"reporting_constraints.pdf","purpose":"Defines the permitted target segments and canonical codes, Irish and Polish statutory rollups, SOX control classes, product-margin requirements, constraint identifiers, and the material-variance policy.","required":true,"discovery":"Use the identified reporting constraints as the authoritative vocabulary for target codes and trace identifiers; the document presents competing requirements rather than a completed crosswalk."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"target_coa_model","filename":"target_coa_model.zip","media_type":"application/zip","description":"Executable dual-legacy chart-of-accounts mapping and period-variance model, containing `coa_model.py` and `README.md`.","required":true,"constraints":["Place the archive at the top level of the working directory. It must contain `coa_model.py` exposing `analyze(records, period_a, period_b)` and `README.md`. Code must run offline under Python 3.11 using only the standard library and must not read the supplied workbook or PDF at runtime."],"rendering_required":false}],"work_activity":"analyze_data","work_product":"analytical_model","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"code_exec@v4","occupation":"accountants_auditors","sector":"professional_scientific_technical_services","task_archetype":"code_exec","estimated_professional_hours":12.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"reference_script","reviewer_policy":"A domain reviewer validates the accounting relationships and constraint traces, while an independent technical reviewer runs the hidden suite in a clean offline Python 3.11 environment. The final score is based on executable behavior plus the stated maintainability and professional-judgment reviews.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The model covers the supplied Irish and Polish account populations and documented products, not a universal chart for future acquisitions.","Statutory rollups and materiality are evaluated against the supplied snapshot rather than live filing guidance.","Narrative quality is reviewed only for traceability, maintainability, and non-prescriptive tone."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:32:12+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:32:12+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:32:12+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:32:12+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R27', 'R28']","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:32:12+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/4551b1fa8e7d0583","declared_deliverables":["target_coa_model.zip"]};
